{%- comment -%}
  LBASS — "PIÈCE UNIQUE" BADGE (2026-08-29)

  WHY THIS SNIPPET EXISTS. The one-of-one signal already existed in markup on
  every surface, but the chip that carries it was rendering as a plain neutral
  outline — visually identical to «متوفرة دابا» (in stock). Two separate places
  had styled it green and BOTH lost the cascade:

      templates/collection.liquid:154   .chip-uniq{background/border-color/color}   (no !important)
      templates/search.liquid:76        style="background:…;color:#37c97a"          (inline, no !important)

  Both lose to snippets/lbass-stamp.liquid:108, which sets

      .chip{ border:…!important; color:…!important; background:transparent!important }

  An !important declaration in a stylesheet beats a normal one at ANY
  specificity — and beats a normal INLINE style too. So the green never
  painted, on either surface. The uniqueness signal was present in the DOM and
  invisible on the page.

  THE FIX follows the house pattern already set by lbass-badge-fix.liquid: win
  on SPECIFICITY, not on load order. Every rule is anchored through a parent
  (.card .lb-uniq = (0,2,0), .pdp-badges .lb-uniq = (0,2,0)) so it outranks the
  token sheet's bare .chip (0,1,0) regardless of what loads when. This snippet
  is ALSO rendered after lbass-stamp in layout/theme.liquid, so it wins on
  order too — belt and braces, because this badge is load-bearing for
  conversion and must not silently die again.

  DESIGN. Red is already spoken for: it is the .lb-stamp die-cut "1/1" on the
  image, the brand signature. This badge is the plain-language explanation of
  that stamp and sits in the spec row, so it takes the SOLID INK plate + bone
  type — the same treatment lbass-badge-fix chose for .pb-grade, and for the
  same reason: a solid plate is the only thing that stays legible against
  unpredictable garment photography. It is the one filled chip in a row of
  outlines, which is exactly the weight the signal should carry.

  COPY. "1/1" is resale jargon. It reads to a reseller and to nobody else, and
  the shop's traffic is general Moroccan retail, not Grailed. The badge says
  «Pièce unique» first — French, plain, the market's second reading language —
  then the Darija. dir="auto" is required: this chip mixes Latin and Arabic on
  an RTL page, the same bidi case the product titles already handle.
{%- endcomment -%}
<style>
/* ── the pièce-unique chip ────────────────────────────────────────────
   Anchored selectors (0,2,0) so the bare .chip (0,1,0) in the token
   sheet cannot take these back. Do not flatten to `.lb-uniq` — that is
   the bug this snippet exists to fix. */
.card .lb-uniq,
.pdp-badges .lb-uniq,
.lbqa-wrap .lb-uniq{
  display:inline-flex!important;
  align-items:center!important;
  gap:5px!important;
  background:var(--lb-ink,#0B0B0C)!important;
  border:1px solid var(--lb-ink,#0B0B0C)!important;
  border-radius:0!important;
  color:var(--lb-bone,#FFFFFF)!important;
  font-family:'Alexandria','Tajawal',system-ui,sans-serif!important;
  font-weight:800!important;
  letter-spacing:normal!important;   /* Arabic: tracking breaks joining */
  line-height:1.3!important;
  white-space:nowrap!important;
  opacity:1!important;
  text-shadow:none!important;
  box-shadow:none!important;
}

/* the leading rule mark — a hairline, not an emoji. Emoji render
   differently across Android/iOS and were already inconsistent in search. */
.card .lb-uniq::before,
.pdp-badges .lb-uniq::before,
.lbqa-wrap .lb-uniq::before{
  content:"";
  width:11px; height:2px;
  background:var(--lb-red,#BF2E15);
  flex:none;
}

/* card + search: sits in the spec row under the title */
.card .lb-uniq,
.lbqa-wrap .lb-uniq{ font-size:11px!important; padding:3px 8px!important; }

/* PDP: the badges row runs larger than the card chips */
.pdp-badges .lb-uniq{ font-size:11.5px!important; padding:6px 10px!important; }

/* The French half is the load-bearing word; the Darija supports it.
   Nested span rather than a second chip so it wraps as one unit. */
.lb-uniq i{ font-style:normal!important; opacity:.72!important; font-weight:700!important; }

@media(max-width:420px){
  /* On the narrowest cards the spec row is already tight — drop the Darija
     rather than let the chip wrap and break the row onto three lines. */
  .card .lb-uniq i,
  .lbqa-wrap .lb-uniq i{ display:none!important; }
}
</style>
